---
const safeguards = [
  {
    title: 'Tenant isolation',
    body: "Each business unit's data is separated in the application and again by database row-level security.",
  },
  {
    title: 'Results held until release',
    body: 'A customer cannot read results while the lab or clinician still has them.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Access audit trail',
    body: 'Views of results, files, and reports are recorded in an append-only log: who, when, and from which request.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Disclosure reports',
    body: 'Admins can export an accounting of disclosures for a patient or an order.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Encryption',
    body: 'TLS in transit. Lab files and the database are encrypted at rest on Azure infrastructure covered by a Microsoft BAA.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Staff MFA and idle logout',
    body: 'Multi-factor sign-in can be required for every staff role, and idle sessions sign out automatically.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Minimal PHI elsewhere',
    body: 'No clinical details are sent to the payment provider, only opaque order and package IDs.',
  },
  {
    title: 'AI with guardrails',
    body: 'In production, report Q&A only uses providers that have been approved as BAA-covered.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Backups',
    body: 'Database point-in-time restore, long-term archives, and versioned lab files.',
  },
];
---

<section class="section soft" id="security">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Security and HIPAA</p>
      <h2>Built toward HIPAA requirements</h2>
      <p>
        Handling lab results means handling protected health information. QiNio is engineered around
        HIPAA's safeguards, and we are open about where that work stands.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid cols">
      {
        safeguards.map((item) => (
          <div class="card">
            <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            <p>{item.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <div class="plain">
      <h3>What we say plainly</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          QiNio is working toward a posture that can be formally assessed. We do not claim a HIPAA
          certification.
        </li>
        <li>
          A Business Associate Agreement is arranged with each customer during onboarding. Each
          business unit remains responsible for its own compliance program.
        </li>
        <li>This page is not legal advice.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .cols {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  }
  .card h3 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }
  .card p {
    margin-top: 8px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.96rem;
  }
  .plain {
    margin-top: 32px;
    padding: 28px 32px;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
    background: var(--bg);
  }
  .plain h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }
  .plain ul {
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    padding-left: 20px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .plain li {
    margin-top: 6px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .cols {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .cols {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
